 e violinist's critically-acclaimed debut album\, <em>STORIES (re)TRACED</
 em> (Orchid Classics)\, explores the intersection of music as a cultural 
 force and folk minority culture and features four seminal and inextricabl
 y connected works for solo violin\, including Béla Bartók's Sonata. Bor
 n in Texas to Chinese immigrant parents\, Zhou began the violin under the
  guidance of her father\, who hails from a family of traditional musician
 s. She went on to study with Miriam Fried at the New England Conservatory
  while pursuing her interest in literature at Harvard University. She now
